    "review": "Approved by the pstack interrogate panel under the owner's delegation of 2026-10-15. Changes from the #234 approval: native is upstream's from-source build of 10.12.0, source 928de8ff918488749ca9d23e0a7349873401b7f7, the Linux x86-64 executable 7b3c74db2c4ce06d2b483813a05c6b5928f81b10c471366d677ec25371b52693 carried by its published target image (pinned below), replacing 10.10.0's fd5ffef2d825d9035b3956b0026911a22e2c1b56f7fa205dd00310cfe88aeff5; restic is unchanged; the uniform runtime is Claude Code 2.1.276 through the gateway provider with claude-opus-5-5 at medium effort, replacing Codex 0.155.0 on Node.js v24.21.0 with gpt-5.6-sol, as the adopted environment dotnet-r4 (manifest SHA-256 cd12d897da384cc4aa802892c7841a7d29bc1c04f883f3f122a6bea0171c673e) carries it with its managed settings; the gateway is sub2api at https://gateway.ai.faviann.com, replacing https://cliproxy.local.faviann.com/v1; and native 10.12.0's software-change graph has four executable nodes instead of six. The review_repair and delivery_repair nodes are gone: a rejected review ends the change iteration through review_retry and a non-ready delivery outcome (ci_failed, conflict, repair_required) through delivery_retry, and the next iteration runs the one worker node with that phase and its feedback, then both reviews and delivery again. Verified: generate.sh, unchanged from #234 and run with that executable copied out of the pinned image, produces these asset bytes twice in clean environments and native admits them with an exact round trip; describe.py, unchanged, reads the structure below (the worker, acceptance, code and deliver nodes, builtin.git-delivery.pr@2 with the v2/pr receipt (ready, ci_failed, conflict, repair_required) whose non-ready outcomes route to delivery_retry, the 10-iteration change loop, no node deadlines, gateway connections on every agent node, GH_TOKEN only on delivery, and the default consider pull-request feedback)."
  },
